# generation: 1
# =============================================================================
#  ketsync.conf — this machine's identity. Copy to ketsync.conf and edit.
#
#  Bump the generation line on EVERY edit. `ketsync sync` refuses to push a
#  file over a newer one, and that number is the only thing that orders them.
# =============================================================================

# master owns the inventory and pushes it. slave receives it.
# Changed BY HAND, on the machine taking over, and only once you are certain
# the other one is not writing - see docs/decisions.md section 2.
KS_ROLE=slave

# the machine that owns the inventory right now. An IP, never a name.
KS_MASTER_IP=10.100.1.17

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ketsync watch - who gets told, and how the watcher itself is watched.
# All four addresses are per-site and REQUIRED before watch runs; it refuses
# without them rather than guessing.
#
# A SLAVE runs watch too, with one question in it: does the master answer.
# The machine that reports the fleet cannot report its own death, so the
# backup node asks that and mails it to KS_MAIL_INFRA - it needs KS_MAIL_FROM
# and KS_MAIL_INFRA (not _NODE, it never sends one) and its own mail-setup.
# KS_MASTER_TRIES / KS_MASTER_GAP (3 tries, 5s apart) are how hard it asks
# before it believes the answer; a blip must not become a page.
#
# Suggested cron:
#   master:  */10 * * * * /root/ketsync/ketsync watch
#            30 7 * * *   /root/ketsync/ketsync watch --digest
#   slave:   */10 * * * * /root/ketsync/ketsync watch
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#KS_MAIL_FROM="ketsync@example.co.th"    # must be a sender the provider VERIFIED
#KS_MAIL_INFRA="infra@example.co.th"     # immediate: backup node, PAUSE, stand-ins live
#KS_MAIL_NODE="node@example.co.th"       # immediate: a node down, a storage left off
#KS_MAIL_DIGEST="admin@example.co.th"    # daily: doctor's full report
# optional dead-man switch (healthchecks.io): green runs ping it, and ONLY
# green runs - a run whose mail failed stays silent so the silence is heard.
#KS_WATCH_HEALTHCHECK="https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>"
#
# The transport: this machine's own sendmail, pointed at an authenticated
# relay by `ketsync mail-setup` (which drives contrib/mail-satellite.sh).
# Any provider speaking authenticated SMTP works - changing provider is an
# edit of these three lines plus `ketsync mail-setup --test`, run again on
# EVERY infra machine that sends (postfix is machine config, not fleet
# config). KEYFILE is the PATH to the key: the key itself lives in one
# root-readable file and never in this conf, this repo, or any container.
#KS_MAIL_RELAY="[smtp-relay.brevo.com]:587"
#KS_MAIL_USER="b5c6b3001@smtp-brevo.com" # Brevo: the GENERATED login, not your
                                         # signup mail. SendGrid: the word apikey
#KS_MAIL_KEYFILE="/root/.brevo.key"      # one line, the bare secret, chmod 0600
